  "description_html": "Skeletal reconstruction of the giant leptoceratopsid <i>Udanoceratops tschizhovi</i>, based on the holotype specimen PIN 3907/11. Postcranial remains are mentioned in the original describing paper but were not described/illustrated.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> A few vertebrae are figured and described in papers by Tereschhenko, and have been referenced for this skeletal.<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-T2008_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T2008-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> <b>Axial length ~3.5 m (11 ft)</b>, which agrees with 3–4 m (9.8–13.1 ft) estimates.<sup id=\"cite_ref-T2008_3-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T2008-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Color_Key\">Color Key</h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#FFFFFF\" title=\"#FFFFFF\"> </b> Known</li>\n<li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#777777\" title=\"#777777\"> </b> Unknown</li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(in Russian) (1992). \"Новый род протоцератопсид из позднего мела Монголии\". <i>Paleontological Journal</i>: 81−93.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(2007). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/226106749\">Key to Protoceratopoid Vertebrae (Ceratopsia, Dinosauria) from Mongolia</a>\". <i>Paleontological Journal</i> <b>41</b>: 175−188. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1134/S0031030107020086\">10.1134/S0031030107020086</a>.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-T2008-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <a href=\"#cite_ref-T2008_3-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-T2008_3-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(2008). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/226432157\">Adaptive Features of Protoceratopsids (Ornithischia: Neoceratopsia)</a>\". <i>Paleontological Journal</i> <b>42</b> (3): 50−64. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1134/S003103010803009X\">10.1134/S003103010803009X</a>.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(2015). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Viktor-Tereshchenko/publication/292476236_Methods_for_size_reconstruction_in_distorted_and_damaged_vertebrae_of_fossil_tetrapods/links/5bdad5264585150b2b960650/Methods-for-size-reconstruction-in-distorted-and-damaged-vertebrae-of-fossil-tetrapods.pdf\">Methods for Size Reconstruction in Distorted and Damaged Vertebrae of Fossil Tetrapods</a>\". <i>Paleontological Journal</i> <b>49</b>: 293−303. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1134/S0031030115030120\">10.1134/S0031030115030120</a>.</cite></span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
